{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Implemented per the 2026-08-16 operator decision; runtime locking behavior unchanged.\n\n- Item 1 (reclaim TOCTOU): accepted and documented. A comment at the os.unlink in _acquire_advisory_lock states the window (nothing excludes another drainer between the stamped_file_is_stale verdict and the unlink), why the mkdir leg is not exposed to it (its caller already holds the exclusive fcntl leg; a single-file lock has no kernel leg to inherit), the bounded harm (redundant drain work only; the per-ticket optimistic queue claim remains the correctness boundary), the retry-once self-limit, and the two conditions that would justify revisiting (drain work ceasing to be idempotent, or the queue claim ceasing to be the correctness boundary). No flock, no create-and-rename.\n- Item 2 (torn-stamp vocabulary): _describe_drain_lock_holder now distinguishes 'no ownership stamp' / 'unrecognised ownership stamp' / 'incomplete ownership stamp', verbatim the phrases doctor_locks._existence_report renders, and renders them as 'an unknown holder (<phrase>)' mirroring doctor's 'unknown (<phrase>)'. The phrases are duplicated rather than imported because the dependency would run llm -> _commands; a new parametrized test (test_drain_and_doctor_describe_a_holderless_lock_identically) pins the two surfaces to the same wording so drift fails a test instead of confusing an operator.\n- Item 3: two new tests in tests/scripts/graph/test_doctor_locks.py assert the drain row's 'unrecognised ownership stamp' and 'incomplete ownership stamp' descriptions (plus holder/pid_state None and the young-lock staleness verdict).\n- Item 4: test_stamp_write_failure_keeps_a_ceiling_bounded_lock forces os.write to raise for the drain lock's fd only, and asserts the fd is still returned, the unattributable-lock WARNING fires, nothing was stamped, and the lock is honoured while young but reclaimed once past the shared wall-clock ceiling.\n\nTDD: the four vocabulary assertions were RED before the change; the item-3/item-4 tests passed on first run, as expected for pure coverage gaps on branches that already existed. make lint and make typecheck green (complexity ratchet: active=49 new=0 increased=0 stale=0). Gerrit change 1918.\n\nDiscovered work filed and linked: moist-short-lionfish (958e-f4b3) - the enrich drain gate check is O(ticket count) and blows its 20 ms budget on every write."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1787175416854411001,"uuid":"c3ff8cee-08c4-449f-874e-1f97292a6709"}